# Development Workflow

Read `docs/development/AI_WORKFLOW.md` for the complete process.

Stay inside the scope of the current task.

Do not implement the next roadmap stage automatically.

Large work must be split into bounded phases. Do not expand scope mid-task because a
related future stage appears in docs.

If you discover useful work outside the task:
- do not implement it;
- report it under `Possible follow-ups`.

For functional stages, work in a feature branch unless the user explicitly says otherwise.

Never:
- force push;
- rewrite main history;
- auto-merge a PR;
- remove existing migrations;
- discard user changes;
- revert or overwrite unrelated uncommitted work.

## Long-running work and interrupts

Acceptance / backfill / full pytest / Docker jobs must use a hard timeout or watchdog.
Do not poll for hours without a deadline, stale detection, and non-zero exit on failure.

Do not leave background agents silently continuing the next scope after the user stops a task.

After an interrupt or aborted background work: first do a recovery audit of the working tree
(status, changed files, what the background task touched). Do not auto-revert unless asked.
Do not start new implementation until the user confirms the recovery plan.

## Checks and reporting

Before declaring work complete, run the relevant real checks:
- backend tests;
- backend lint;
- frontend tests;
- frontend production build;
- Docker validation/health when runtime was changed.

Do not claim a test passed unless it was actually executed.

Ordinary automated tests must not rely on live MOEX, CBR, Polza, or other external APIs.

At completion report:
- Implemented
- Tests
- Git
- Deviations
- Issues
- Possible follow-ups

Then stop and wait for the next task.
